  "instruction": "Design an astable 555-timer LED blinker schematic from scratch and save it as `/home/user/Desktop/answer.sch`. Start EAGLE from `/opt/eagle-7.7.0/bin/eagle` and open the supplied board or schematic there. Requirements: 1. The output must be a well-formed EAGLE schematic XML file. 2. It must contain at least one `<part>` whose `deviceset` or `device` matches `555` case-insensitively. 3. It must define parts with refdes `R1`, `R2`, `C1`, `C2`, and either `LED1` or `D1`. 4. It must include at least one VCC supply part and at least one GND supply part. 5. It must contain at least 3 `<net>` elements. 6. `R1` and `R2` must have non-empty plausible resistor values such as `10k` or `2.2M`, and `C1` must have a non-empty plausible capacitor value such as `10u`, `100n`, or `47nF`.",
